          "blocks": {
            "accordion_row_e6jTk8": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What will I need to order my prescription lenses?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_LDD8wt": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>You will need your prescription and PD (pupillary distance) measurement. Any optician can provide you with these and you are under no obligation to purchase your glasses from your optician. We will need to know if you are after distance or readers (single vision lenses) or if you need them for both and have multifocal lenses (progressive lenses).</p><p><strong>We require all prescriptions to be within the last 12 months. We suggest customers upload their scripts to ensure all prescription information is delivered accurately to our lab. </strong></p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_LDD8wt"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_HtAKVC": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How do I obtain my prescription?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_jPJDXm": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>To obtain an eye prescription, schedule a comprehensive eye exam with a licensed optometrist or ophthalmologist. Following the refraction test, the doctor is legally required to hand you a physical or digital copy of your prescription at no extra charge. If you already had an exam, simply call your eye doctor's office to request a copy.<br/></p><p>You are not under any obligation to purchase your glasses from your optician - so do not feel pressured into doing so!</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_jPJDXm"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_iPHmzK": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What are progressive lenses?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_qbLWmC": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Progressive lenses are Multifocal lenses with different sections of vision correction. With a seamless transition in the lens from distance on top, to reading correction at the bottom, they can provide much sharper overall vision.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
